Leona and kelp meet at a concert 
Kelp: Leona, hey!
Leona: Sugar, hi! This venue is quite the spot you chose, such a gorgeous view. You listen to The Sharks often? 
Kelp: They’re bangers! I’ve been a fan since their first album. I love “Yellow Car.” Here, I got us sweet tea brine, they said it was freshly brewed.
Leona: I love that song. Oh, this is good. You just earned yourself some serious points, darlin’. Swam up right to the top of my list.
Kelp: Glad I passed the test.
Leona: Test? That was just the warmup. I found us the perfect spot between the brain coral and the sea fan cluster. The acoustics bounce off the reef wall. I love the lyrics to this song. Talking about the open ocean. Why tie yourself down when the whole sea is out there for you? 
Kelp: I don’t think roots tangle you up, I planted roots and everything I wanted grew up around me. There’s a world of difference between tied down and anchored. 
Leona: That’s real different from how I see it, but neither one of us is wrong, sugar. Kelp, you are one of the finest creatures of the reef, truly. You were made for something already built and loved, but I was made for the open ocean. I don't think I'm looking for someone to share my life with, baby. I think I just love my life.
Kelp: That might be the most beautiful thing I’ve heard all night and the music was really good.
After date
Kelp: Leona and I just swim in different styles and that’s okay.
+0 satisfaction. Neither heartbroken, neither fulfilled 
Leona: It’s so freeing being able to choose myself. I enjoy being independent, darlin’ that’s just how my fins flow.
+5 satisfaction. Fulfilled  

